Compilation, smoke testing, and episode verification pass, but the new animated inserts omit sound events for repeated or intermediate motion. This causes audible/visual desynchronization in the generated reels.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Emit an impact for every guichet cycle — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\lcdg\inserts.py:4582-4584
  When the scene lasts longer than two cycles, `image()` keeps replaying the form movement via `t % g["cycle"]`, but `sons()` schedules only two impacts. Longer guichet inserts therefore visibly repeat without synchronized collision sounds; generate events until `self.fin` instead of using a fixed `range(2)`.

- [P2] Sound each falling box — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\lcdg\inserts.py:4396-4397
  For `boites > 2`, `image()` animates every box at its own `_t(i)`, but `sons()` produces only one sound at the first box and one at the last. The intermediate box drops are silent, so the new addition motion is not synchronized with its sound effects.
